  "evaluation": "C is best: it grounds the apparent disagreement in a full depression scale versus a depression dimension of a quality-of-life measure, matching the rules’ outcome_measure exception, and also identifies the reversed score-direction label. B correctly explains that both reported results indicate improvement, but relies only on score direction rather than explicitly identifying the different scope of measurement. A makes the same correct directionality observation but is slightly less precise about the measurement distinction. All three correctly retain the vitamin D combination interventions as on-question and identify relevant secondary differences.",
